title "Easier-to-scan links page"
why   "The links page was hard to scan, so each link now shows its site and there is a message when the list is empty"
from  diff, tests, session

screen   page  "Links page"
endpoint api   "Links API"
table    links "links"
page -> api "fetches"
api -> links

~ page "Each link shows its site name"
    + site name under the title
    ~ long titles cut short with "…"
    say "Under each link's title you now see which website it is from, like github.com, in small grey text."
    eng "row() parses l.url with new URL(), strips a leading www. from hostname, renders it in span.site; titles are ellipsised via .text a CSS."
    proof public/index.html:26
    proof public/index.html:41
    said "The links page is hard to scan. Show each link's site name and favicon"
+ part icon "Letter circle"
    + first letter of the site
    + colour picked from the site name
    say "Next to each link there is a coloured circle with the site's first letter; the same site always gets the same colour."
    eng "28px .icon span, border-radius 50%, white text; background hsl(hue(site) 55% 45%) where hue() is a simple string hash mod 360. Replaces the favicon the first request asked for."
    proof public/index.html:22
    proof public/index.html:32
    said "Just show the first letter of the site in a coloured circle instead."
+ part empty "No links yet message"
    say "When nothing is saved yet, the page says so and tells you how to add your first link."
    eng "Static <p id=empty hidden>; load() sets hidden = links.length > 0 after every list refresh."
    proof public/index.html:18
    proof public/index.html:55
    said "show a friendly message when there are no links yet"
= page "Makes no requests to outside services"
    say "The page does not fetch website icons or anything else from other sites, so no one outside learns which links are saved."
    eng "An earlier draft in this session loaded <origin>/favicon.ico from each linked site; that was removed entirely. No external URLs, images or scripts remain in index.html."
    proof public/index.html:21
    said "Don't load favicons from Google or any outside service, privacy matters to us."
= api "Server and database untouched"
    say "Nothing changed in how links are saved, listed or deleted."
    eng "server.js and db.js are not in the diff; the existing API tests still pass."
    proof test adds and lists links
    proof test deletes a link
! page "Behaviour changes nobody asked for"
    say "Titles and web addresses are now shown as plain text, and links that are not normal web addresses are listed but can no longer be clicked. This closes a hole where a saved title could run code on the page."
    eng "Rendering switched from an innerHTML template to createElement/textContent (fixes stored XSS via title/url); a.href is set only for http: and https: URLs, so javascript: and invalid URLs are not clickable. Not covered by any test; only reasoned about."
    proof public/index.html:37
    proof public/index.html:38
! page "Never seen in a browser"
    say "Please open the page once with no links and once with a few: nobody has looked at the new layout yet, and white letters on some circle colours (yellows, greens) may be hard to read."
    eng "Verified only that the inline script parses and that GET / serves the new HTML; no UI tests exist. Check contrast of #fff on hsl(h 55% 45%) for h around 50-90 and the empty-state toggle after deleting the last link."
    proof public/index.html:32
